{"id":"n-20261009-emjocw","category":"tech","display_title":"From Tech Executive to Spiritual Guide","display_title_he":"מבכיר הייטק למורה דרך רוחני","short_summary":"An Israeli tech entrepreneur leaves the corporate world after building successful companies to lead spiritual journeys in nature.","english_level":"C1","words":512,"reading_time":4,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"Ynet","domain":"ynet.co.il","url":"https://www.ynet.co.il/economy/article/rj5nnzgigg","title":"אחרי שני אקזיטים ההייטקיסט הפך למורה דרך: \"הייתי עצבני, לא רציתי לקום בבוקר\"","published_at":"2026-10-09T05:04:08.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-09T05:04:08.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-09T06:26:44.538Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Transitioning from a high-pressure career in the high-tech industry to a life centered on nature and spirituality, Erez Goldstein has redefined his personal and professional path. At 59 years old, Goldstein spent decades managing software and cybersecurity firms, including roles as CEO of SoftCubes BI and the software division of One1, a public group with over 7,000 employees and thousands of clients, as well as managing security sectors at Oracle Israel. Despite reaching senior leadership positions, he began to feel a deep internal restlessness and chronic stress. He noted that despite external financial and career achievements, he felt persistently preoccupied, lacked inner peace, and realized his employees felt his stress.","In 2011, Goldstein established Integrity Software, specializing in software marketing and cybersecurity infrastructure. Starting without external funding and relying entirely on personal savings, he made a firm commitment to himself not to attend job interviews for a full year. After six months without revenue, orders eventually started coming in like the first winter rain. Seven years later, in 2018, he sold a two-thirds stake of Integrity Software to Matrix for millions of shekels, making it a subsidiary while he continued working as CEO. Furthermore, in 2022, his cybersecurity startup Crusoe Security was acquired by the American security giant Palo Alto Networks.","Yet, even amidst these significant business milestones, the emotional toll and the larger existential questions lingered. Deciding that he no longer wanted to wake up exhausted and anxious, Goldstein embarked on a lengthy personal transformation. Over an 18-year period, he engaged in diverse studies, exploring Yamima cognitive thinking for self-awareness, ancient Jewish wisdom, Kabbalah, Hasidic philosophy under teachers like Dov Elboim without religious markers, and a niche of shamanism. He gradually realized that his true calling lay beyond corporate boardrooms and financial portfolios.","In October 2021, Goldstein stepped down as CEO of Integrity Software, transitioning to a part-time presidency before eventually selling his remaining shares to Matrix. Today, he dedicates the vast majority of his time to his new initiative, named 'Adam and Earth Journey', though he still spends one day a week on business, such as leading the CISO IL club of over 200 chief information security officers. The project invites small groups of up to twenty participants—often influential figures in business, media, and academia, with less than ten percent acceptance rate—on a seven-weekend experiential program across Israel. Participants hike through locations ranging from watching the sunrise at Timna Park, traversing the southern craters and the Judean Desert, connecting with history in the Golan Heights and Upper Galilee, to finishing in Jerusalem with ritual immersion in a spring and walking up to the Temple Mount through the City of David.","While Goldstein acknowledges that achieving this lifestyle transition required substantial financial security built during his years in tech, and that dreaming big has its costs, he volunteers his time for the venture, charging participants only for logistics. By combining his business acumen with being a certified Israeli tour guide, he hopes to help others find profound mental well-being and life purpose rather than merely chasing professional milestones, treating nature as a powerful stage for learning."],"facts":[{"fact":"Erez Goldstein is a 59-year-old Israeli tech entrepreneur and former executive who held leadership roles at SoftCubes BI, Oracle Israel, and One1.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"In 2011, Goldstein founded Integrity Software without external investment, committing to a year without job interviews using personal savings.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"In 2018, Goldstein sold two-thirds of Integrity Software to Matrix, turning it into a subsidiary while remaining CEO.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"In 2022, his cyber startup Crusoe Security was acquired by American cybersecurity giant Palo Alto Networks.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Despite career success, Goldstein experienced inner restlessness and stress, prompting a gradual shift toward ancient Jewish wisdom, Kabbalah, shamanism, and Yamima thinking.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Goldstein stepped down as CEO of Integrity in 2021, later became president, and eventually sold his remaining shares to Matrix to focus on spirituality and his new venture 'Adam and Earth Journey'.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"His venture 'Adam and Earth Journey' offers small groups a seven-weekend experiential program combining nature hikes across Israel with mental and spiritual exploration.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Transitioning","lemma":"transition","pos":"verb","he":"מבצע מעבר","name":false},{"text":"high-pressure","lemma":"high-pressure","pos":"adjective","he":"עתיר לחץ","name":false},{"text":"career","lemma":"career","pos":"noun","he":"קריירה","name":false},{"text":"industry","lemma":"industry","pos":"noun","he":"תעשייה","name":false},{"text":"centered","lemma":"center","pos":"verb","he":"ממוקד","name":false},{"text":"nature","lemma":"nature","po